          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: weshalb",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "weshalb — \"why, for what reason\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Niemand weiß, weshalb der Laden heute geschlossen ist. Nobody knows why the shop is closed today."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A question word like warum. In an indirect question it sends the verb to the end: …, weshalb er geschlossen ist."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "weshalb joins wes, the old genitive of was \"what\", to halb in its old sense \"on the side of, because of\": \"because of what\". EtymDB has no entry, so this follows the usual account."
            }
          ]
        },
